  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#child-browsing-context-name-property-set\n\n> the value of the name content attribute for all a, applet, area, embed, form, frameset, img, and object elements that have a non-empty name content attribute and are in a document tree with window's browsing context's active document as their root; and\n\nThis section of the specification does not seem to match the behavior of the browsers I tested using:\n- http://w3c-test.org/html/browsers/the-window-object/named-access-on-the-window-object/named-objects.html\n\nFirefox / WebKit: returns only applet, embed, form, img, and object.\nBlink: returns only embed, form, img, and object. (Looks like Blink does not expose HTMLAppletElement on window so they may have dropped its support entirely)\n\nThe specification says we should also return a, area and frameset but no browser seems to do this (I haven't tested Edge).\n\nShould we align the specification with major browsers and drop \"a, area and frameset\" from this text?\n",
